WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.472 --> 00:00:06.041
- [DRock] I'll see
you in four hours.

00:00:06.041 --> 00:00:07.178
- See you DailyVee.

00:00:07.178 --> 00:00:09.332
See you in four hours.

00:00:09.332 --> 00:00:11.486
(rap music)

00:00:42.316 --> 00:00:43.957
Alright, I gotta 
make this quick call.

00:00:43.957 --> 00:00:45.478
(static)

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.850
(engine revving)

00:00:49.919 --> 00:00:52.009
(silence)

00:00:58.759 --> 00:01:00.394
- You know and the whole
place is obviously open--

00:01:00.394 --> 00:01:01.728
- I just, I just
need to have a--

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:04.164
- float through.

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:04.998
- Two or three times a year

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.967
I want to do a real wine
event that matters,--

00:01:06.967 --> 00:01:07.634
- Yeah.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.469
- and this is the
place to do it.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:12.775
Six weeks ago or so

00:01:12.775 --> 00:01:14.975
I was in a meeting here 
in LA and all the

00:01:14.975 --> 00:01:17.210
gentleman I was with, 
I was with Lindsay and

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.745
we were with David, 
one of her mentors.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.547
He said, "You guys have
a few minutes today?"

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:22.649
And we're like, "Well,
we can make it happen.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.217
"What's going on?"

00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:25.919
He's like, "You have come
and see this amazing place."

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:30.123
So we readjusted our schedules
in the middle of a kind of a

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:34.294
weekday drove down here and
were introduced to this amazing

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.954
gentleman that I'm excited to

00:01:35.954 --> 00:01:38.484
introduce many of you 
to but others know.

00:01:38.484 --> 00:01:40.214
We did a little bit of a tour 
that I know many of

00:01:40.214 --> 00:01:42.436
you have already done before.

00:01:42.436 --> 00:01:43.971
I was completely blown away.

00:01:43.971 --> 00:01:46.610
Even more exciting to me is
as we were going through the

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:51.037
incredible wonderland that he's
created here in the middle of LA

00:01:51.037 --> 00:01:52.980
I kinda looked at the 
space we're in and I said,

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:56.750
"You know for a long time I've
been wanting to put together a

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:00.087
"wine dinner in LA and have a
mix of my friends and

00:02:00.087 --> 00:02:01.989
acquaintances get together 
and get to know each other."

00:02:01.989 --> 00:02:04.858
So something that's been
bouncing around in my mind for

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:09.029
the last 18 months or so came
together when I saw this spot

00:02:09.029 --> 00:02:10.964
and this incredible
energy that's created here.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.332
So I'm having a lot of fun

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:14.735
watching you guys kind
of mix-and-match.

00:02:14.735 --> 00:02:16.565
(light pop music)

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:20.807
Cheers.
Thank you.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.309
Get home safe, love you all.

00:02:22.309 --> 00:02:22.976
Thank you.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.104
Cheers. Cheers.

00:02:25.814 --> 00:02:26.880
Nice.

00:02:29.759 --> 00:02:31.885
- Was fun.
- That was fun.

00:02:57.226 --> 00:02:58.414
- [Blurred Man] Gary!
- [Gary] Hey bro.

00:02:58.414 --> 00:03:00.732
- [Blurred Man] What up, dude?
- [Gary] Sorry, I'm late.

00:03:03.223 --> 00:03:05.452
I think if you love process,

00:03:05.452 --> 00:03:07.057
and you're comfortable 
with adversity,

00:03:07.057 --> 00:03:08.989
if you have the stomach for it,

00:03:08.989 --> 00:03:10.330
and you love the journey

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:14.528
over the fruits and 
riches of that journey

00:03:14.528 --> 00:03:16.496
you now have the two
foundational pieces

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.632
to be a successful
entrepreneur.

00:03:18.632 --> 00:03:20.400
You know, right now
entrepreneurship

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.469
is on this 
interesting pedestal.

00:03:22.469 --> 00:03:23.904
All of you want to be one.

00:03:23.904 --> 00:03:25.476
Everyone wants to be one.

00:03:25.476 --> 00:03:27.415
But the truth is, it sucks.

00:03:27.415 --> 00:03:28.739
It's hard.

00:03:28.739 --> 00:03:29.997
Almost everybody loses.

00:03:29.997 --> 00:03:32.411
Almost everybody loses

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:35.469
and that is not something we're
having a conversation around.

00:03:35.469 --> 00:03:39.186
You genuinely have 
to like getting beat up.

00:03:39.186 --> 00:03:42.255
You generally have 
to like the conflict.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:46.679
You generally have to have an
enormous amount of patience

00:03:46.679 --> 00:03:48.829
to really actually pull it off.

00:03:48.829 --> 00:03:52.332
In a world where everybody now
gets to play in social media,

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.934
you create a profile,
you're in the game.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:56.369
In a world where
everybody gets an at-bat,

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.938
we're about to realize that

00:03:57.938 --> 00:04:01.374
the far majority of
people aren't good enough.

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:03.376
You know we haven't had to
quantify this before because

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:05.445
there were people 
in place to filter people

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.380
that America got to see

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.484
and most of them were 
qualified to some level and

00:04:10.484 --> 00:04:13.520
so all we ever saw in
the news and the media

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:18.190
was a curated .0001% of us and

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.892
of that 90% weren't good enough

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.195
because the human that 
decided that was flawed.

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.131
Now what we have 
is an ecosystem

00:04:24.131 --> 00:04:26.600
where everybody's getting out
there and saying they're great.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.703
The problem is far majority
aren't going to be great

00:04:29.703 --> 00:04:32.205
at what they pontificate 
at being great at

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:35.631
and we're gonna watch them
fail in front of our eyes.

00:04:35.631 --> 00:04:39.546
(light R&amp;amp;B music)

